            <ArticleTitle>Diverticulitis of the appendix, a distinctive entity: preoperative diagnosis by computed tomography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>609-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10140-015-1328-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diverticular disease of the appendix is rare and is usually diagnosed during surgery. We report a case of a 50-year-old man who presented to the emergency department with right lower quadrant pain of 1-day duration. A preoperative diagnosis of appendiceal diverticulitis was made by computed tomography of the abdomen. The patient underwent emergency laparoscopic appendectomy, which confirmed the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
